# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "10. Compare fidelities of original and postselected noisy states {#10-compare-fidelities-of-original-and-postselected-noisy-states}"
msgstr "10. Bandingkan fidelity keadaan berhingar asal dan yang dipilih-pasca {#10-compare-fidelities-of-original-and-postselected-noisy-states}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We see that postselecting only samples with no detected errors greatly improves the expectation value for every stabilizer, and thus improves the estimated fidelity of the stabilizer state. Although the postselected values were calculated using only the samples that passed every check, the expectation values are much more accurate and the sampled variance is lower. We can also now see that the postselection rate above was actually converging to a value similar to the noisy circuit fidelity. The postselection rate was converging because the checks were catching the vast majority of errors actually occurring during circuit execution.\n"
msgstr "Kita melihat bahawa pemilihan-pasca hanya sampel tanpa ralat dikesan sangat meningkatkan nilai jangkaan bagi setiap penstabil, dan dengan itu meningkatkan anggaran fidelity keadaan penstabil. Walaupun nilai pemilihan-pasca dikira menggunakan hanya sampel yang lulus setiap semakan, nilai jangkaan jauh lebih tepat dan varians sampel lebih rendah. Kita juga kini dapat melihat bahawa kadar pemilihan-pasca di atas sebenarnya menumpu kepada nilai yang serupa dengan fidelity litar berhingar. Kadar pemilihan-pasca menumpu kerana semakan menangkap sebahagian besar ralat yang sebenarnya berlaku semasa pelaksanaan litar.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice/guides/low-overhead-error-detection-using-spacetime-codes/extracted-outputs/post-select-plots-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice/guides/low-overhead-error-detection-using-spacetime-codes/extracted-outputs/post-select-plots-1.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice/guides/low-overhead-error-detection-using-spacetime-codes/extracted-outputs/post-select-plots-2.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice/guides/low-overhead-error-detection-using-spacetime-codes/extracted-outputs/post-select-plots-2.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since one set of checks serves every stabilizer, there is a single gamma curve to look at: the value of the cost function after each check was committed. For other problems on a different set of physical qubits, and with an imperfect noise model (remember, our noise model in this tutorial exactly modeled the noise affecting the samples), the order in which checks are added to the target qubits can have a more pronounced effect on how the curve converges.\n"
msgstr "Memandangkan satu set semakan digunakan untuk setiap penstabil, hanya terdapat satu lengkung gamma untuk dilihat: nilai fungsi kos selepas setiap semakan dikomit. Bagi masalah lain pada set qubit fizikal yang berbeza, dan dengan model hingar yang tidak sempurna (ingat, model hingar kita dalam tutorial ini memodelkan dengan tepat hingar yang menjejaskan sampel), urutan semakan ditambah pada qubit sasaran boleh memberi kesan yang lebih ketara terhadap cara lengkung itu menumpu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This gamma curve converging to ``1.0`` implies that additional checks will not be able to detect a great deal of additional error, as there is very little modeled error that is uncovered by the checks. This reinforces our earlier observation regarding convergence in postselection rate being due to a lack of uncovered error in the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Lengkung gamma yang menumpu kepada ``1.0`` ini membayangkan bahawa semakan tambahan tidak akan dapat mengesan banyak ralat tambahan, kerana terdapat sangat sedikit ralat termodel yang tidak dilindungi oleh semakan. Ini mengukuhkan pemerhatian kita sebelum ini bahawa penumpuan kadar pemilihan-pasca disebabkan oleh ketiadaan ralat yang tidak dilindungi dalam litar.\n"

